.TH CORTEX 1 "April 2026" "cortex-memory 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cortex \- three-layer semantic memory system for AI assistants
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cortex
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fIlevel\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Cortex
is a Python CLI tool that provides a three-layer semantic memory system for
AI coding assistants. It uses vector embeddings via Ollama for semantic search
and stores memories in ChromaDB, organised across working, episodic and
semantic layers. It can also be driven via the MCP protocol (JSON-RPC 2.0
over stdio or SSE) for direct integration with AI agents.
.PP
Install via PyPI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pip install cortex-memory
# or run without installing:
uvx cortex
.fi
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create
Create a new memory.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fIstring\fR
Memory title (derived from content if omitted)
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-content " " \fIstring\fR
Memory content (required)
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-level " " \fIlevel\fR
Memory level: working, episodic, semantic (default: episodic)
.TP
.BI \-\-tags " " \fItags\fR
Comma-separated tags
.TP
.BI \-\-session " " \fIid\fR
Session ID (required for working level if not auto-derived)
.TP
.BI \-\-source " " \fIsource\fR
Source: manual, auto, llm (default: manual)
.TP
.BI \-\-task\-id " " \fIid\fR
Task or ticket ID
.TP
.BI \-\-author " " \fIstring\fR
Author identifier
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output result as JSON
.RE
.TP
.B search \fIquery\fR
