.SH MEMORY LAYERS
Cortex organises memories in three layers:
.TP
.B working
Short-lived, session-scoped notes. Automatically scoped to a session ID
derived from the current git branch.
.TP
.B episodic
Medium-term memories covering specific tasks, bugs, and decisions.
.TP
.B semantic
Long-term distilled knowledge: patterns, conventions, architecture decisions.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .agents/cortex/config.yaml
Project-local configuration file
.TP
.I .agents/cortex/
ChromaDB storage directory (default)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All environment variables follow the
.B CORTEX_
prefix and mirror the YAML configuration hierarchy
(e.g.\&
.B CORTEX_STORAGE__PATH
overrides
.I storage.path
).
Notable variables:
.TP
.B CORTEX_STORAGE__BACKEND
Storage backend (default: chroma)
.TP
.B CORTEX_STORAGE__PATH
Storage directory path (default: .agents/cortex)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS__PROVIDER
Embeddings provider (default: ollama)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS__MODEL
Ollama model name (default: nomic-embed-text)
.TP
.B CORTEX_EMBEDDINGS__ENDPOINT
Ollama API endpoint (default: http://localhost:11434)
.TP
.B CORTEX_SEARCH__TOP_K
Default number of search results (default: 5)
.TP
.B CORTEX_SEARCH__MIN_SCORE
Default minimum similarity score (default: 0.5)
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an episodic memory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex create \-\-content "Use refresh tokens for better security" \\
  \-\-level episodic \-\-tags jwt,auth
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a working-layer note for the current session:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex create \-\-content "Investigating flaky test in CI" \-\-level working
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search memories semantically:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex search "authentication issues" \-\-top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Consolidate knowledge into the semantic layer:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex consolidate "Always validate JWTs server-side" \-\-level semantic
.fi
.RE
.PP
Promote working memories to episodic at session end:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex transfer\-working
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export all memories to Markdown:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex export \-\-all \-\-output ./memories.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start MCP server for AI agent integration:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex start\-mcp\-server \-\-transport stdio
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install the man page to your local share:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cortex install\-man
.fi
.RE
.SH MCP INTEGRATION
The MCP server exposes tools for AI agents including:
.BR cortex_search ", " cortex_create ", " cortex_list ", " cortex_get ", "
.BR cortex_consolidate ", " cortex_promote_memory ", " cortex_update_memory ", "
.BR cortex_mark_obsolete ", " cortex_review_session ", "
.BR cortex_think_about_memory_maintenance ", " cortex_think_about_task_completion ", "
.BR cortex_choose_memory_layer .
.PP
The MCP server communicates via JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio (default) or SSE.
